%I A399571 #16 Sep 16 2026 17:11:18
%S A399571 191,251,397,773,1097
%N A399571 Primes p such that 2^p-1 has a divisor d with 1<d<2^p-1 and d == 1 (mod 2*p^2).
%C A399571 a(6) >= 1213.
%C A399571 2657, 12589, 13679, 49043 and 93077 are also terms.
%H A399571 Mers Project, <a href="https://mers.sourceforge.io/lowM.txt">Known information for Mersenne numbers with exponents below 200000</a>.
%H A399571 S. S. Wagstaff, Jr., <a href="https://homes.cerias.purdue.edu/~ssw/cun/pmain126.txt">Main Tables from the Cunningham Project</a>.
%e A399571 For a(1)=191, d = 7068569257*332584516519201 = 2350896688821832838803657 is a proper divisor of 2^191-1 and d == 1 (mod 2*191^2).
%e A399571 For p=93077, d=11686604129694847=2*674487*93077^2+1 is a prime divisor of 2^93077-1.
%o A399571 (PARI) isok(p) = { if(!isprime(p), return(0)); my(M=2^p-1); fordiv(M, d, if(1<d && d<M && (d-1)%(2*p^2)==0, return(1))); return(0); }
%Y A399571 Cf. A001348, A065341, A135975, A398494.
%K A399571 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A399571 1,1
%A A399571 _A. Lamek_, Sep 03 2026
